From bea7e8cb5963a74ecc60ba611e6db9c7874319e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gf691271 <gf691271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:26:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: stop re-opening a stream that is already open
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on the night of 2026-11-16 (5,644 packets of 0x19/0x05): the largest gap between
two consecutive packets was 42 s, and the "silences" the CSV report are not missing packets
at all — the device keeps sending every ~14 s, with timestamp 0 and every slot rri=0, i.e.
the PPG has no pulse to report. 110 of 148 packets inside the 62-minute gap were like that.

Meanwhile the 15 s re-open produced 1,304 writes in one night, and 194 of the 236 error
answers on this channel (code 0x0001E84A) arrived within 10 s of one of them: the device was
rejecting "open" on a stream that was already open. The error rate peaks in the same hour as
the empty packets (02:00: 25 % of that hour's frames).

The window tick now asks the device to open only when the channel is genuinely quiet:

  nothing at all since the window opened, past the 5 min grace  -> drop the link
  no packet for 15 min                                        -> drop the link
  no packet for 90 s, or nothing yet in this window            -> send one open
  otherwise                                                    -> do nothing

90 s is twice the largest measured gap. A stream that is merely beatless needs nothing:
lastRriPacketMs is refreshed by every packet, empty ones included.

Compiled: assembleMainlineDebug BUILD_OK.

Also measured this session, for the record:
- 0006 keepalive verified on device: screen off + force-stop + am start does not connect
  (autoconnect=false), and 18.5 min later KeepAliveReceiver fired and connected in 1 s.
- The 11-15 loss was "screen off + general_autoconnectonbluetooth=false": the app never even
  logged "Will attempt to connect", because the activity never resumed.
---
 .../devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java | 32 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java b/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java
index e8d2390..655ced9 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/nodomain/freeyourgadget/gadgetbridge/service/devices/huawei/HuaweiSupportProvider.java
@@ -342,6 +342,20 @@ public class HuaweiSupportProvider {
     private static final long RRI_LIVENESS_GRACE_MS = 5 * 60 * 1000L;
     /** The long sleep pauses reach 12 min, so a reconnect is attempted at most this often. */
     private static final long RRI_LINK_DROP_COOLDOWN_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000L;
+    /**
+     * Local patch: how long the beat stream may be silent before the open request is sent
+     * again.
+     *
+     * Measured over one full night (2026-11-16): 5,644 packets, the largest gap between two
+     * consecutive 0x19/0x05 packets was 42 s. A stream that is quiet for 90 s has therefore
+     * really stopped, while one that is merely reporting no beats keeps sending empty
+     * packets (timestamp 0, all slots zero) and needs nothing.
+     *
+     * Re-opening every 15 s as before produced 1,304 writes per night, and 194 of the 236
+     * error answers on this channel (code 0x0001E84A) arrived within 10 s of one of them:
+     * the device was rejecting "open" on a stream that was already open.
+     */
+    private static final long RRI_REOPEN_AFTER_SILENCE_MS = 90 * 1000L;
     private long windowEnteredMs = 0L;
     private boolean rriOpenedThisWindow = false;
     private long lastLinkDropMs = 0L;
@@ -359,18 +373,24 @@ public class HuaweiSupportProvider {
                 if (windowEnteredMs == 0L) {
                     windowEnteredMs = now;
                 }
-                if (!rriOpenedThisWindow && now - windowEnteredMs > RRI_LIVENESS_GRACE_MS) {
-                    // The stream never produced a packet in this window. Either the open request
-                    // never landed or the link is dead; both are fixed by reconnecting.
+                // Every 0x19/0x05 arrival refreshes lastRriPacketMs, empty packets included,
+                // so this is "did the channel carry anything", not "did we get beats".
+                boolean heardSinceWindow = lastRriPacketMs >= windowEnteredMs;
+                long silenceMs = now - lastRriPacketMs;
+                if (!heardSinceWindow && now - windowEnteredMs > RRI_LIVENESS_GRACE_MS) {
+                    // Nothing at all since the window opened: the open request never landed or
+                    // the link is dead. Reconnecting is the fix for both.
                     LOG.info("RRI_LINKSTALE no packet since window start, dropping connection");
                     dropDeadLink(now);
                     windowEnteredMs = now;
-                } else if (rriOpenedThisWindow && now - lastRriPacketMs > RRI_LIVENESS_MS) {
+                } else if (silenceMs > RRI_LIVENESS_MS) {
                     LOG.info("RRI_LINKSTALE last packet {}s ago, dropping connection",
-                            (now - lastRriPacketMs) / 1000);
+                            silenceMs / 1000);
                     dropDeadLink(now);
                     windowEnteredMs = now;
-                } else {
+                } else if (!heardSinceWindow || silenceMs > RRI_REOPEN_AFTER_SILENCE_MS) {
+                    // Ask again only when the channel is actually quiet. While the device is
+                    // streaming (even with empty packets) a new request is rejected.
                     openRriStream();
                 }
             } else if (now - lastRriPacketMs < 120_000L && now - rriLastCloseMs > 300_000L) {
